  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "At a certain time of day, a flagpole casts a shadow 15 m long, and at the same time a stick 30 cm high casts a shadow 24 cm long. Assuming that both the stick and the flagpole are perpendicular to the horizontal ground, find the height of the flagpole.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$18.75\\text{ m}$.",
      "worked": "The two right triangles have the same angle of sunlight at the same time, so they are similar by AAA. Using the same units in the stick ratio, $\\frac{h}{15}=\\frac{30}{24}$. Hence $h=15(\\frac{30}{24})=18.75\\text{ m}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
